    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-17 (round 15).**\n\n**Symptom.** Running `hypergumbo sketch -t 2000 .` on any repo emits:\n\n```\nhypergumbo also created comparison sketches temporarily:\n  4x budget (8,000t):  /tmp/hypergumbo_sketch_compare/sketch.8000.withsource.md\n  16x budget (32,000t): /tmp/hypergumbo_sketch_compare/sketch.32000.withsource.md\n\nTo preserve them to cache:\n  cp /tmp/hypergumbo_sketch_compare/sketch.8000.withsource.md /home/jgstern_agent/.cache/hypergumbo/.../sketch.8000.withsource.md\n  cp /tmp/hypergumbo_sketch_compare/sketch.32000.withsource.md /home/jgstern_agent/.cache/hypergumbo/.../sketch.32000.withsource.md\n```\n\nThe text claims \"temporarily\" but the files are not cleaned up.\n\n**Verified problems.**\n\n1. **Accumulation, no cleanup.** Observed contents of `/tmp/hypergumbo_sketch_compare/` on 2026-05-17:\n   - 27 files, ~30 MB total\n   - Oldest file `sketch.12800000.withsource.md` (18 MB) dated 2026-04-21 — almost 4 weeks old\n   - Files persist across runs; no producer ever deletes them\n\n2. **Shared state across repos.** Filenames are based ONLY on token budget (e.g. `sketch.8000.withsource.md`), not on repo path. Different repos race-overwrite the same path:\n   - Single-file Python tmp repo run: `sketch.32000.withsource.md` 322 bytes at 00:25\n   - Test-only tmp repo run: same path overwritten to 318 bytes at 00:26\n   - If a user runs sketches on two repos and tries to follow the \"preserve\" suggestion, they'll cp the WRONG repo's comparison sketch into their cache.\n\n3. **Misleading UX.** Telling the user to manually `cp` files INTO their own cache directory (`~/.cache/hypergumbo/<hash>/...`) leaks internal cache management. Either auto-preserve them or don't generate them.\n\n4. **Disk hygiene.** Combined with INV-padum (cache balloon: 7.9 GB / 76 entries / 1 repo / 3 days), this is another silent disk-growth source on dev machines.\n\n**Reproduction.**\n```bash\nmkdir -p /tmp/r15repo && echo \"def f(): pass\" > /tmp/r15repo/a.py\nhypergumbo sketch -t 2000 /tmp/r15repo\nls -la /tmp/hypergumbo_sketch_compare/   # 27 files, oldest from Apr 21\n```\n\n**Fix.** Three reasonable options:\n1. Write comparison sketches into `~/.cache/hypergumbo/<repo-hash>/<state-hash>/` directly (auto-preserve), so each repo's comparison sketches are isolated and survive across runs.\n2. Use repo-keyed filenames in `/tmp/hypergumbo_sketch_compare/<repo-hash>/sketch.NNN.withsource.md` and clean up on each run for that repo.\n3. Just delete the manual `cp` UX entirely and only generate comparison sketches when explicitly requested.\n\n**Severity.** Medium — operational hygiene. Silent disk growth + cross-repo collision risk + misleading \"temporarily\" wording.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n- INV-padum (cache balloon: 7.9 GB) — same family of \"no cleanup policy\"\n- WI-nijum (Generated N UX wart) — related sketch output noise\n\n**Notebook reference.** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05162026_0438.md` Round 15 section (to be appended)."  # 2001
